+{"body":"Fixes #522.\n\n`SplitMemoryLinks` now finds links with an internal source and an external target when using its default source linked list. Exact enumeration, counting, and `SearchOrDefault` agree with `UnitedMemoryLinks`; `GetOrCreate` returns the existing link.\n\n### Reproduction and cause\n\nCreate point 1, then link 2 with source 1 and target `new Hybrid<ulong>(20, isExternal: true).Value` (18446744073709551596). Asking for `[any, 1, externalTarget]` should find link 2: `any` leaves the link's own ID unrestricted.\n\n| Operation on the split store | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Read link 2's source and target directly | Correct stored values | Correct stored values |\n| `Each(any, 1, externalTarget)` | `[]` | `[2]` |\n| `Count(any, 1, externalTarget)` | `0` | `1` |\n| `SearchOrDefault(1, externalTarget)` | `0` | `2` |\n\nAn index is a lookup table for finding links by their endpoints. The united store keeps data and index metadata in one memory region, with store-wide source and target trees. The split store separates data from metadata and selects indexes using the configured external-reference range. Its default internal-source index is a linked list; external targets have a store-wide target tree.\n\nThe stored link was correct, but both exact-query branches searched the external **source** tree. That tree indexes external sources, so it had no entry for source 1. The two branches now search the external **target** tree, which contains link 2. The source-tree configuration already chose a suitable internal tree and continues to pass.\n\nAs requested, I studied [doublets-rs PR #75](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/pull/75), including its C# comparison. Rust chooses internal/external indexes based on whether an ID exists, so its repair moves entries when an ID is created. C# chooses by a configured address range; this failure needs only the two corrected tree selections.\n\n### Tests and release preparation\n\n- Added 20 regression cases. Before the fix, all 12 linked-list cases failed while eight source-tree controls passed. All 20 now pass.\n- Separate cases verify `Each`, `Count`, and `SearchOrDefault` with `byte`, `ushort`, `uint`, and `ulong` addresses, default settings, and recursive/recursionless size-balanced trees with source lists or trees.\n- Full-scan comparisons cover all four internal/external endpoint combinations, absent pairs, wildcard queries, `Break` callbacks, endpoint changes, deletion, ID reuse, and `GetOrCreate`.\n- Added a [runnable united/split example and explanation](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/tree/issue-522-2819acda0f21/examples/ExternalReferences). Both stores now print `Each -> [2], Count -> 1, SearchOrDefault -> 2` on .NET 8 and .NET 10.\n- Prepared NuGet patch version **0.18.2** and release notes; packing produces the package and symbols successfully.\n- Enabled the C# workflow on pull requests, including the example, with .NET 8 setup and finite hang/job limits. Publishing and documentation jobs run only on main pushes. Updated retired action versions and the deprecated workflow output command in that workflow.\n\n### Validation\n\n```sh\ndotnet test csharp/Platform.Data.Doublets.sln -c Release -f net8 --blame-hang-timeout 3m\ndotnet test csharp/Platform.Data.Doublets.Tests -c Release --filter FullyQualifiedName~SplitMemoryExternalReferencesTests\ndotnet run --project examples/ExternalReferences -c Release\ndotnet pack csharp/Platform.Data.Doublets -c Release --no-build\n```\n\nLocal validation: .NET 8.0.427 full solution run **40 passed, 1 existing skipped test** (`ScopeTests.FullAutoResolutionTest`, already marked “Would be fixed later.”). The focused regressions also pass on SDK 10.0.112/runtime 10.0.12. The example passes on both runtimes. Package contents confirm version 0.18.2, the updated release notes, and README. `actionlint`, all Markdown rules for the example README, and `git diff --check` pass. Existing compiler/documentation/package warnings remain.\n\nOn commit `f06746345dbd8024127517c6ae20b722f372c381`, [C# CI run 40671503061](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/actions/runs/40671503061) passes the full suite and example; release/documentation jobs are correctly skipped on the PR. [Auto-merge workflow run 40671500003](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/actions/runs/40671500003) also passes. [Codacy static analysis](https://app.codacy.com/gh/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/pull-requests/523) passes with zero new issues. Current main is included, the complete PR diff has been reviewed, and the working tree is clean.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-28T10:02:48Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-28T10:02:48Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/issues/522","messageHeadline":"Initial commit with task details","oid":"f19b2af81428ff691002019f6a95ac34782e9b6a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-28T10:11:09Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-28T10:11:09Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Fix split-memory lookups for internal sources and external targets","oid":"7634c9039eaffbf10c387d5b3b33467e33174031"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-28T10:11:09Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-28T10:11:09Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Run C# tests and external-reference example on pull requests","oid":"9d95bd9e856bd391871873cbbb8f3ec1e58575f6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-28T10:17:50Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-28T10:17:50Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Address Codacy findings in regression tests and example","oid":"8d6090506ad180e0f4d5e30ffe0022b041301a6e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-28T10:21:36Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-28T10:21:36Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Add example title metadata for Markdown validation","oid":"f06746345dbd8024127517c6ae20b722f372c381"}],"title":"[C#] Fix split-memory lookups with internal sources and external targets","url":"https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets/pull/523"}
